# Binary Builders Website Guidelines
# Single-page presence site built with Vite + TypeScript

## Core Principles
- Keep the site a single page
- Prefer vanilla TypeScript over frameworks
- Keep markup semantic and accessible
- Optimize for performance

## Code Standards

### HTML
- Use semantic HTML5 elements
- Maintain 2-space indentation
- Use double quotes for attributes

### CSS
- Follow BEM naming convention
- Use 2-space indentation
- Use CSS custom properties for theme values
- Write mobile-first media queries

### TypeScript
- Use ES6+ features
- Follow camelCase naming for variables and functions
- Maintain 2-space indentation
- Use double quotes for strings
- Always use semicolons
- Prefer const over let, avoid var

## Project Structure
/src            # TypeScript and CSS
/pub            # Static files copied as-is (Vite publicDir)
index.html      # Page shell
vite.config.ts  # Build config (outDir: dist)
